# Lunara Homeschool Quest – Project Rules

## Tech stack (this project only)
- **Framework:** Next.js 16 (App Router), React 19, TypeScript
- **Data & Auth:** Supabase only (Postgres, Auth, Storage). No GraphQL, Apollo, or Grafbase in this repo.
- **Styling:** Tailwind 4, custom design system (`design-system.css`, `globals.css`), Quicksand + Macondo fonts
- **State:** Server components + server actions for mutations; client state/localStorage for kid done state and gamification cache

## Conventions
- **Data reads:** Use `@/lib/supabase/data.ts` (server) or direct Supabase client in server components.
- **Data writes:** Use `@/lib/supabase/mutations.ts` (server-only) or server actions in `@/lib/actions/*`. Never write from client with anon key for sensitive operations.
- **Kid session:** Kid login is cookie-based (`lunara_kid_session`). Middleware restricts kids to `/kids/[theirId]/*` and redirects away from `/parent`. Use `getKidSession()` and service role client when acting on behalf of a kid.
- **Timezone:** Always use the parent/family timezone for “today” and date boundaries (e.g. kid portal, reports). Fetch from the kid’s family (e.g. profile timezone of a family member). Default to `America/Chicago` only when no timezone is set. Do not hardcode timezone in UI logic.

## Patterns
- Match existing file structure and naming (e.g. `ScheduleItemsList`, `getScheduleItemsForStudent`).
- Use existing UI components and design tokens (e.g. `--ember-*`, `--celestial-*`, `btn-primary`).
- Prefer server components; use `'use client'` only when needed (hooks, events, browser APIs).
- Keep strong typing (types in `@/types`, Zod for API/forms where used).

## What not to do
- Do not introduce Apollo, Grafbase, or GraphQL in this project.
- Do not assume “authenticated user” on kid portal routes; use kid session or service role for kid-scoped data.
- Do not hardcode timezone for “today” or week boundaries; use parent/family timezone.
